From 842bca7fc1714de50d1ac1e928b557356a588d2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samaBR85 <sama85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:53:13 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] input: HD Rumble and DualSense haptics through RenHDrum

Routes the controller vibration of the SDL driver into RenHDrum
(https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum): Switch Pro Controller / Joy-Con get
5 ms AM/FM HD Rumble packets, a wired DualSense gets 48 kHz audio haptics on
its voice coils. SDL3 3.4.8 is built from source with RenHDrum's two
HD Rumble transport patches (no-queue / write-after-input).

Port of the Brontide reference patches 0002-0007 by Three-Dola
(integrations/brontide in RenHDrum, GPL-3.0-or-later) to an Eden-family
tree, with the conflicts resolved by hand. msvc_compat.cpp from 0002 is
left out: it only works around static Qt prebuilts.

